		poiPathAlarmSuppressionPoiCTA OBJECT-TYPE
			SYNTAX CTA
			MAX-ACCESS read-only
			STATUS current
			DESCRIPTION
				"Topology address of the corresponding POI module to which the POI path belongs to.
				
				The corresponding POI subrack and slot numbers have to be calculated out of the POI address. 
				The POI address is the integer number following the equal sign ('=') of the CTA string. 
				
				POI-SR = ( (POI_address - 1) / 8 ) + 1 where '/' represents a integer division with remainder
				POI-Slot = ( (POI_address - 1) % 8 ) + 1 where '%' represents a modulo operation
				
				E.g. 
				CTA = 'POI=1'  is located in POI-SR 1  slot 1
				CTA = 'POI=64' is located in POI-SR 8  slot 8
				CTA = 'POI=65' is located in POI-SR 9  slot 1
				CTA = 'POI=80' is located in POI-SR 10 slot 8
				CTA = 'POI=81' is located in POI-SR 11 slot 1"
			::= { poiPathAlarmSuppressionEntry 1 }
		
